# Docker build-context excludes.
#
# This file must live at the REPOSITORY ROOT: the documented build command
# (packaging/docker/Dockerfile.serve:8) uses `.` as the context, and Docker
# reads .dockerignore from the context root only — one next to the Dockerfile
# would be ignored.
#
# Without it, the builder stage's `COPY . .` bakes the entire working tree into
# an image layer, including every path .gitignore deliberately protects:
# provider API keys in .env*, session transcripts and MCP OAuth tokens under
# .stella/private/, the full .git/ history, and a multi-GB /target.
#
# Patterns are matched against the path relative to the context root, so a bare
# `.stella/` excludes only the top-level one — the tracked
# bench/readiness/.../app/.stella/ fixture is untouched, which is what we want.
#
# DO NOT exclude a workspace member (root Cargo.toml `members`, including
# bench/loop-bench): cargo needs every member manifest present to load the
# workspace, even when building a single --bin.

# Build output and VCS history
target/
.git/

# Local secrets and per-workspace private state
.env
.env.*
.stella/
.oxagen/
.memories/

# Agent/session scratch — never repository content, and never image content
.claude/
.agents/
.agents.d/
.agent/
sandbox/
verifications/

# Docs site and its node_modules — not part of the cargo build
stella-docs/
docs/
node_modules/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
